            {
              "role": "label",
              "name": "Decides when a dual-role key counts as a hold if another key is pressed. Rules can override this default in advanced options. Chord detection is configured separately.\n\nAfter another key is released: the key becomes a hold once another key is pressed and released while it is down, or when the hold threshold passes. Fast rolls while typing stay taps.\n\nAs soon as another key is pressed: useful for dedicated layer or modifier keys. Reacts faster, but overlapping letters while typing can trigger the hold by mistake.",
              "description": "",
